WEBVTT

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:03.933
Calendars keep everyone's time in one place:

00:00:03.933 --> 00:00:08.978
company events, your own meetings, a team's schedule, and the rooms people book.

00:00:08.978 --> 00:00:13.378
This video shows the kinds of calendars, how to open the calendar and

00:00:13.378 --> 00:00:17.660
read your week, how to add, change, cancel and delete an event, and

00:00:17.660 --> 00:00:20.300
how to look at someone else's schedule.

00:00:24.900 --> 00:00:28.499
Every calendar has a type that says what it is for.

00:00:28.499 --> 00:00:34.749
A General calendar is shared and belongs to nobody in particular, such as a company calendar.

00:00:34.749 --> 00:00:38.600
A Personal calendar is your own, and everyone gets one.

00:00:39.350 --> 00:00:43.303
A Team calendar belongs to a role, so everyone in the team sees

00:00:43.303 --> 00:00:44.850
it and can add to it.

00:00:44.850 --> 00:00:49.204
Room and Equipment calendars hold the bookings of a meeting room or of

00:00:49.204 --> 00:00:53.730
something you reserve, and an Office calendar shows who is in the office.

00:00:54.480 --> 00:00:57.298
Each type offers its own kinds of events.

00:00:57.298 --> 00:01:02.035
A personal calendar has Event, Meeting, Focus time and Out of office, and

00:01:02.035 --> 00:01:04.973
a team calendar adds On call and Milestone.

00:01:04.973 --> 00:01:10.130
Which types you can choose depends on the features your administrator turned on.

00:01:14.303 --> 00:01:16.699
Open Calendars, then Calendar.

00:01:16.699 --> 00:01:22.422
The first time anyone opens it, a personal calendar named after them is created.

00:01:22.422 --> 00:01:29.543
Maria sees hers, maria.lopez, next to the shared Company calendar and her team's Sales Team calendar.

00:01:29.994 --> 00:01:34.087
The list on the side shows every calendar you can see, each with

00:01:34.087 --> 00:01:35.841
the color of its events.

00:01:35.841 --> 00:01:39.876
Tick a calendar to show its events, and untick it to hide them.

00:01:39.876 --> 00:01:42.214
The browser remembers your choice.

00:01:42.665 --> 00:01:46.356
Day, Week, Month and Agenda change the layout.

00:01:46.356 --> 00:01:52.815
Month shows the whole month at once, and Agenda lists the events one after the other.

00:01:53.267 --> 00:01:57.268
The arrows move back and forward, and Today comes back to today.

00:01:57.268 --> 00:02:01.269
Times are shown in your time zone, from your user profile or the

00:02:01.269 --> 00:02:04.927
site, so they match the rest of the site wherever you are.

00:02:09.101 --> 00:02:11.400
To add an event, choose New event.

00:02:11.400 --> 00:02:15.309
When you can add to more than one calendar, you first pick the

00:02:15.309 --> 00:02:17.436
calendar and the kind of event.

00:02:17.436 --> 00:02:20.311
Let's add a meeting to Maria's own calendar.

00:02:20.783 --> 00:02:23.872
The editor opens in a window over the calendar.

00:02:23.872 --> 00:02:27.778
Give the event a Title, check the Kind of event, and set when

00:02:27.778 --> 00:02:29.235
it Starts and Ends.

00:02:29.235 --> 00:02:32.733
A Category can color the event and lets you filter it.

00:02:33.209 --> 00:02:37.986
Further down are the time zone, the Location and a Description, the Status,

00:02:37.986 --> 00:02:42.763
and Show as, which can mark an event as Free so it doesn't block your time.

00:02:42.763 --> 00:02:47.539
Visibility can make an event private, so others only see that you are busy.

00:02:47.990 --> 00:02:49.137
Choose Save.

00:02:49.137 --> 00:02:54.300
The window closes and the calendar shows the new event on Friday afternoon.

00:02:55.742 --> 00:02:58.636
You can also drag across the times you want.

00:02:58.636 --> 00:03:03.036
The editor opens with those times already filled in, so only the title

00:03:03.036 --> 00:03:04.310
is left to type.

00:03:04.310 --> 00:03:07.552
Choose Save, and the new event is on the calendar.

00:03:11.756 --> 00:03:15.917
Click an event to see its calendar, its kind and its status.

00:03:15.917 --> 00:03:18.376
Edit opens it in the same window.

00:03:18.826 --> 00:03:23.378
Change what you need, here the time it starts and ends, and choose Save.

00:03:23.378 --> 00:03:25.596
The event moves on the calendar.

00:03:26.049 --> 00:03:29.557
You can also drag an event to another day to move it, or

00:03:29.557 --> 00:03:32.725
drag its bottom edge to make it longer or shorter.

00:03:32.725 --> 00:03:36.799
If a move isn't allowed, the event goes back and you are told why.

00:03:37.249 --> 00:03:41.624
To cancel an event, open it, choose Edit, and then Cancel event.

00:03:41.624 --> 00:03:46.248
It no longer shows on the calendar, and the people invited are told.

00:03:46.248 --> 00:03:50.622
Delete, next to it at the bottom of the editor, removes an event

00:03:50.622 --> 00:03:55.059
for good, and a repeating event goes with all of its occurrences.

00:03:59.260 --> 00:04:03.943
Maria is a manager, so she also has Whose schedule under the calendar list.

00:04:03.943 --> 00:04:08.858
Choose people, pick one or more users in the box that appears, and choose Show.

00:04:08.858 --> 00:04:13.831
The calendar shows the events on their own calendars and the events they attend.

00:04:13.831 --> 00:04:16.780
Moving to next week shows when they are busy.

00:04:18.476 --> 00:04:23.731
The events she isn't allowed to open appear as Busy, with their time but no title.

00:04:23.731 --> 00:04:27.075
Back to my calendars returns to her own calendars.

00:04:27.075 --> 00:04:30.836
Only people with the right permission see Whose schedule.

00:04:32.836 --> 00:04:37.062
Pick the calendars to show, switch the view, add events from a click

00:04:37.062 --> 00:04:41.288
or a drag, change, cancel or delete them, and look at other people's

00:04:41.288 --> 00:04:43.572
schedules when you are allowed to.

00:04:43.572 --> 00:04:45.056
Thanks for watching.

